#: {{ux|en|He was on '''cloud nine''' for days after she agreed to marry him.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Watchman Nee|authorlink=Watchman Nee|chapter=Living by Faith|title=The Salvation of the Soul: Translated from the Chinese|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Christian Fellowship Publishers|year=1978|page=107|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=kEC9BQAAQBAJ&pg=PA107|isbn=978-0-935008-31-9|passage=In your zeal you may not feel you are undertaking a thing for your own sake but think you are doing so for God. Nevertheless, you should remember that at the time of great excitement as though you were on '''cloud nine''', you may perhaps be most fleshly!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Shirlee Emmons|authorlink=Shirlee Emmons|author2=Alma Thomas|chapter=Postperformance Management|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=NQfxYpPwLhoC&pg=PT395|title=Power Performance for Singers: Transcending the Barriers|location=New York, N.Y.; Oxford|publisher={{w|Oxford University Press}}|year=1998|isbn=978-0-19-511224-5|passage=Following a highly successful tour of Italy in July/August 1993, with recital and orchestral appearances and an especially inspiring last performance, I returned to New York on '''cloud nine''' and full of euphoria.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Eknath Easwaran|authorlink=Eknath Easwaran|chapter=12|title=A More Ardent Fire: From Everyday Love to Love of God|location=Tomales, Calif.|publisher=Nilgiri Press|month=May|year=2000|page=142|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=dxcNUISHyXEC&pg=PT142|isbn=978-1-888314-03-8|passage=Most of us do not think of excitement as a problem. After all, doesn't everybody like to be on '''cloud number nine'''? I agree: if we could stay on '''cloud number nine''', life might be very pleasant. But, as all of us know, the cloud eventually evaporates. Then we not only come abruptly back to earth; we usually burrow right into its depths and hide&nbsp;– that is, we go into a depression.|brackets=on}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Melissa de la Cruz|authorlink=Melissa de la Cruz|chapter=Not Quite Ready for Her Close-up|title=Lip Gloss Jungle|series=Ashleys|seriesvolume=4|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Aladdin Paperbacks|Aladdin Mix]]|year=2008|isbn=978-1-4169-3409-7|title2=Popularity Takeover|series2=The Ashley Project|location2=New York, N.Y.|publisher2=Aladdin Mix|month2=April|year2=2015|pages2=176–177|pageurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=uM7BAwAAQBAJ&pg=PA177|isbn2=978-1-4814-0974-2|passage=A. A. scanned the crowd and spotted Lili's happy face. Lili had been on '''cloud nine''' ever since she and Max had gotten back together.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Thumbiko Shumba|chapter=1|title=Worklife|location=Pittsburgh, Pa.|publisher=RoseDog Books|year=2010|page=1|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=DszzRX6M4G8C&pg=PA1|isbn=978-1-4349-4578-5|passage=On the first day at the university I was on '''cloud nine''' that I had begun my intellectual life. I was happy to join the cream of creams.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|possibly|nonstandard}} A state of [[fantastic]] or [[impractical]] [[dreaming#Noun|dreaming]] or [[thinking#Noun|thinking]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=W. E. Cushen|chapter=The Management of Change|editors=Frances C. Bell and Harold F. Wollin|title=Report of the 55th National Conference on Weights and Measures 1970: Sponsored by the National Bureau of Standards; Attended by Officials from the Various States, Counties, and Cities, and Representatives from U.S. Government, Industry, and Consumer Organizations, Salt Lake City, Utah, July 13–17, 1970|series=NBS Special Publication|seriesvolume=342|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=[[w:National Institute of Standards and Technology|National Bureau of Standards]], {{w|United States Department of Commerce}}|date=16 July 1970|year_published=April 1971|page=152|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=NXQGJdQ7u04C&pg=PA152|oclc=681216774|passage=Now, the system approach, needless to say, wants to help out in that particular problem, but it lives up on '''cloud nine''' for the most part. This is one of the reasons that it has not made more headway than it has in the civilian agencies of government.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Robert Schindler|chapter=Puget Sound Region—Establishing a Continuing Program [Question Period]|editor=Jacob Silver|title=Geographic Base File System—Establishing a Continuing Program: Conference Proceedings: January 18 and 19, 1973, Seattle, Wash.|series=Computerized Geographic Coding Series|seriesvolume=GE60 no. 4|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=[[w:United States Census Bureau|Bureau of the Census]], Social and Economic Statistics Administration, [[w:United States Department of Commerce|U.S. Department of Commerce]]|month=May|year=1973|page=26|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=6C8mAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA26|column=2|oclc=3256256|passage=Mr. Walsh&nbsp;– {{...}} It sounds like the purpose of the geographic base coding system is to fulfill a planning function of the agency. If that is not the case, then I am concerned as that is one way to get up on "'''cloud nine'''"—that is, to not associate with end products.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Basil Arthur|authorlink=Basil Arthur|title=Appropriation Bill—Financial Statement|journal=Parliamentary Debates (Hansard): Third Session, Thirty-ninth Parliament: [[w:New Zealand House of Representatives|House of Representatives]]|location=Wellington, N.Z.|publisher=P. D. Hasselberg, government printer|date=28 July 1981|volume=439 (Comprising the Period from 17 July to 7 August 1981)|page=2049|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=r2IrAQAAIAAJ&pg=PA2041|oclc=191255532|passage=Members are living on '''cloud nine''' if they think that playing the stock-numbers game is doing anything for the farmers or the country.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Murray N[ewton] Rothbard|authorlink=Murray Rothbard|chapter=War, Peace, and the State|title=Egalitarianism as a Revolt against Nature and Other Essays|edition=2nd|location=Auburn, Ala.|publisher=[[w:Mises Institute|Ludwig von Mises Institute]]|year=2000|pages=115–116|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=WhGCDVK_Kq0C&pg=PA115|isbn=978-0-945466-23-9|passage=By coming to grips with these problems, we can demonstrate that libertarianism is not just a beautiful ideal somewhere on '''Cloud Nine''', but a tough-minded body of truths that enables us to take our stand and to cope with the whole host of issues of our day.}}

